  "notes": [
    "Pin anchors were projected from the existing 2D servo connector map.",
    "Verify connector socket alignment in the 3D Asset Lab before promotion.",
    "Power: SG90 class micro servos typically use 4.8-6 V on VCC; do not power the motor load from an Arduino GPIO pin.",
    "Current: running current is load-dependent and stall current can exceed the Arduino 5 V regulator budget, so use an external 5 V supply when the servo may move under load.",
    "Grounding: when an external servo supply is used, connect the external supply GND and Arduino GND together so the PWM signal has a common reference.",
    "External power: recommended when the servo moves under load or when more than one servo is connected.",
    "Common ground: when an external servo supply is used, connect the external supply GND and Arduino GND together so the PWM signal has a common reference."
